      "doi": "10.1007/BF01413460",
      "journal": "Zeitschrift fur Physik A - Atoms and Nuclei",
      "notes": "Collinear laser-ion beam spectroscopy on all 7 stable Ba+ isotopes. Table 1 (p. 127): isotope shifts relative to 138Ba for the 493.4 nm (6s 2S1/2 - 6p 2P1/2) and 455.4 nm (6s 2S1/2 - 6p 2P3/2) transitions. Table 2 (p. 127): A and B hyperfine constants for 135Ba and 137Ba in 6s, 6p 2P1/2, and 6p 2P3/2 levels. Sign convention: delta_nu^{138,A} = nu_A - nu_138 (positive for lighter isotopes). The 455 nm isotope shifts are the primary high-resolution measurement of that line. The 493 nm data are superseded by Hucul et al. 2017 (same values, more isotopes). The A and B constants are less precise than Villemoes et al. 1993.",
      "data_types": ["isotope_shift", "hyperfine_constant"]
    }
